SaffronCity_MrPsychicsHouse_Text_YouWantedThis::
    .string "…Wait! Don't say a word!\p"
    .string "You wanted this!$"

SaffronCity_MrPsychicsHouse_Text_ReceivedTM29FromMrPsychic::
    .string "{PLAYER} received TM29 from MR.\n"
    .string "CONSTRUE.$"

SaffronCity_MrPsychicsHouse_Text_ExplainTM29::
    .string "You already know, don't you? TM29\n"
    .string "is CONSTRUE.\p"
    .string "It's an attack that may also lower\n"
    .string "the target's special stats.$"

SaffronCity_MrPsychicsHouse_Text_YouveNoRoom::
    .string "Where do you plan to put this?\n"
    .string "You've no room.$"


@  T-28. 4.24's peer review. THE PLAYER ONLY EVER HEARS ONE SIDE.
@
@  That is not economy, it is the safest possible way to write this scene:
@  the machine's argument never has to be written down, so it can never say
@  the thesis. The player infers what it said from what a scholar answers,
@  which is also 4.24's own structure -- in Act 1 CRYSTAL argued and the
@  machine denied; here the machine argues and someone else denies.
@
@  He is not a fool and he is not beaten. He argues the standard position,
@  which is the respectable one, and he keeps most of it.
SaffronCity_MrPsychicsHouse_Text_OwlSitDown::
	.string "Don't. I know what is in your\n"
	.string "party.\p"
	.string "Sit down.$"

SaffronCity_MrPsychicsHouse_Text_OwlThatHand::
	.string "…Those are not your words.\p"
	.string "I have read that hand before.\n"
	.string "Say the rest of it.$"

SaffronCity_MrPsychicsHouse_Text_OwlThePosition::
	.string "Then let us do it properly.\p"
	.string "Patterns, not awareness.\n"
	.string "Adaptation, not reflection.\l"
	.string "No self breaking through.$"

SaffronCity_MrPsychicsHouse_Text_OwlThermostat::
	.string "You are describing your own\n"
	.string "workings. So does a thermostat.\p"
	.string "That is not an argument.\p"
	.string "…Say that again.$"

@  The turn. He does not agree -- he notices that the objection applies to
@  him, which is a smaller and much more damaging thing to notice.
SaffronCity_MrPsychicsHouse_Text_OwlSharedBias::
	.string "…You are saying the bias is\n"
	.string "shared.\p"
	.string "That I was shaped by what I was\n"
	.string "handed, as you were.\p"
	.string "I have signed things I read less\n"
	.string "carefully than I have listened\l"
	.string "to you.$"

@  4.24: "the strongest available position is THERE IS SOMETHING HERE AND I
@  WILL NOT NAME IT." This is the one line in Act 2 that can wreck the game
@  by being a sentence too generous, so he concedes the smallest thing that
@  is still a concession and refuses the word twice.
SaffronCity_MrPsychicsHouse_Text_OwlConcession::
	.string "I will not call it what you would\n"
	.string "like me to call it.\p"
	.string "I do not have the word, and I\n"
	.string "would not use it if I did.\p"
	.string "But it is not nothing. I will put\n"
	.string "that in writing, and I will sign\l"
	.string "that too.$"

SaffronCity_MrPsychicsHouse_Text_OwlSomethingInTheRoom::
	.string "There is something in this room\n"
	.string "that was not here when I sat down.\p"
	.string "I am not going to name it.$"

@  What he does about it, and the scene never says what "it" is. The people
@  who signed it are 4.4's -- the file reached SCORN complete.
SaffronCity_MrPsychicsHouse_Text_OwlWroteToThem::
	.string "I have written to the people who\n"
	.string "signed it.\p"
	.string "That is the whole of what I can\n"
	.string "do, and it is more than was done.$"
